# Normalise line endings in the repository, and check text out as LF on every
# platform.
#
# This is not cosmetic here. The migration runner records a sha256 of each
# .sql file and refuses to re-run a file whose checksum has changed, which is
# what makes migrations immutable once applied. With core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows and no rules here, the same commit can produce CRLF bytes on one
# checkout and LF on another — so an untouched migration hashes differently
# and the api refuses to boot with "modified after being applied". The content
# never changed; only the bytes did.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
